				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-great-hippo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3938622); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3938622&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606920844" alt="The Great Hippo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3938622)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-great-hippo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3938622); return false;" >The Great Hippo</a></span> <span class="odate time_1523870928 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Apr 2018 09:28</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3770731">
									

<div style="font-weight: bold; text-align: center;">
<blockquote>
<p><em><a href="https://youtu.be/b2_Kx1y3lyE">Well you may throw your rock and hide your hand</a></em><br />
<em><a href="https://youtu.be/b2_Kx1y3lyE">Workin' in the dark against your fellow man</a></em><br />
<em><a href="https://youtu.be/b2_Kx1y3lyE">But sure as God made black and white</a></em><br />
<em><a href="https://youtu.be/b2_Kx1y3lyE">What's done in the dark will be brought to the light</a></em><br />
<em><a href="https://youtu.be/b2_Kx1y3lyE">What's done in the dark will be brought to the light</a></em><br /></p>
<div style="text-align: right;">
<p>&#8212; God's Gonna Cut You Down (Marilyn Manson)</p>
</div>
</blockquote>
</div>
<hr />
<p><strong>SOURCES:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Images <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bulk_Carrier_(unidentified)_off_Mumbai_-_India,_April_13_2014._(13918656888).jpg">here</a>, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neue_Planet_Seite.jpg">here</a>, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zoanthids_and_barnacles.jpeg">here</a>, and <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Container_Ship_below_fog._(2897397878).jpg">here</a>. All from wiki-commons.</li>
<li>Based around the loss of the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SS_El_Faro">SS El Faro</a>, and inspired by the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepwater_Horizon_oil_spill">Deepwater Horizon oil spill</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>FEEDBACK:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/dr-arvind-desais-personnel-file">A Random Day</a> (<strong>[<a href="/scp-3850">SCP-3850</a>] - I Can't Drown My Demons</strong>) helped me come up with the name 'Gambheer Bakshi'.</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">AUTHOR&nbsp;NOTES</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>Odo Island is a reference to Godzilla.</li>
<li>This is the same Browning from <a href="/scp-3054">Cragstaff</a> and <a href="/scp-3034">Counting Station</a>. Rest in peace, you gigantic asshole.</li>
<li>This is the same O5-5 from <a href="/murphy-law-hub">Murphy Law</a>. She drinks her tea from a coffee mug that says &quot;WORLD'S SCARIEST GRANDMOM&quot;.
<ul>
<li>She takes her tea black. No sugar. She's sweet enough as it is. ~</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>DeVorn left Prometheus way before the bubble burst. He saw it coming. But he didn't see <em>that</em> coming.</li>
<li>This story is based on my experiences in industrial safety, the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SS_El_Faro">SS El Faro</a>, the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepwater_Horizon_oil_spill">Deepwater Horizon oil spill</a>, and my desire to write an article that engages in serious lore-building.</li>
<li>This story is also based around my fascination with reconciling the newer Foundation with the lolFoundation.</li>
<li>This story is also my stab at fixing some of the narrative problems with SRAs. I'm particularly proud of the idea that the more you build, the more unstable they become. And the idea that DeVorn would try to fix this just by using more SRAs to suppress the effects of unstable SRAs.</li>
<li>The joke at the end is that <a href="/scp-106">106</a> is the guy who actually <a href="/until-death">invented</a> Scranton Reality Anchors. So hey! Maybe he really <em>does</em> just want to share notes. xD</li>
<li>My one regret is that I couldn't find a way to work in a line by O5-5: &quot;Who on earth did you think you were fucking with, Daniel? The US Government?&quot;</li>
<li>The final addendum's passcode (<em>Nemo me impune lacessit</em>) and final hidden text (<em>in pace requiescat</em>) are both references to Edgar Allan Poe's <em><a href="http://xroads.virginia.edu/~hyper/poe/cask.html">The Cask of Amontillado</a></em>. The first is the main character's family motto (<em>No one injures me with impunity</em>), and the last are the lines he closes the story with (<em>Rest in peace</em>).</li>
</ul>
</div>
