			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3770751">
									

<p>I'm about to head to bed, so I didn't read 100% of the page, but this seems really interesting! I love the language used in dialogue, it's much more natural than the typical dialogue on this site (which tends to be really contrived and unnatural in flow). I wish more people wrote dialogue like this. Just to give constructive stuff, though:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;bullshit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;bullshit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>When you say &quot;all anomalous behavior ceases after leaving SCP-3241&quot;, do you mean the boat, or the area around SCP-3241? The boat should likely be named SCP-3241-A or something along those lines, as it seems to be a part of the SCP at this point.</li>
<li>Some more detail could be used when describing SCP-3241 itself, as only one short paragraph is used. What does it look like? What does it appear to be made of? What are some anomalies it exhibits?</li>
<li>You should write &quot;Sommerfeld Assessment and Containment Group (SARC)&quot; the first time SARC is used, not the last time. Additionally, it should be written like that instead of: &quot;SARC (Sommerfeld Assessment and Containment Group)&quot;, as notes in parenthesis typically give a colloquial term like &quot;Dwayne Johnson (The Rock)&quot;</li>
<li>You likely don't have the copyright to that first image. It belongs to TOTE Maritime.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Great work from what I've read, though! I love the themes of debate and corruption.</p>
<p>edit: just realized this isn't a draft, and you weren't asking for critiques. oops.</p>

